--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Android host (android/): Kotlin application that extracts the staged runtime,
  starts an embedded Node.js 18.20.4 (nodejs-mobile, small-icu) on 127.0.0.1 and
  shows the UI in a WebView. All application data stays in the app-private
  directory.
* Server patches, inline in SillyTavern/ and marked with `// ST-ANDROID`:
  skip webpack at startup, accept Node 18, and answer git-only extension
  operations with 501 because no system git exists on the device.
  scripts/verify-patches.sh checks the behaviour of these patches, not just
  their presence.
* A floating, draggable settings control replaces the pinned corner button.
* Data export/import (zip), log viewer, and build/release automation
  (.github/workflows/).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Corresponding source
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

https://github.com/snake-aabb-wtf/sillytavern-android

Every released APK is built by CI from a tag in this repository. The tag holds
the exact source of the Android host, the patched SillyTavern tree, the runtime
staging scripts and the workflow that produced the APK. The bundled
assets/runtime.zip is generated by scripts/stage-runtime.sh from SillyTavern/
plus its npm dependencies, which are present in this repository.

No changes are made to the licence terms of the upstream project.
